For transformer-based world models \citep{micheli2023iris}, whether this boundary shifts remains open. The environment-dependence extends to remedy efficacy: intervention configurations calibrated on Walker fail on Cheetah despite identical DoF, where CIVO severity is $2$--$20\times$ higher (\S\ref{sec:remedies}), underscoring that morphology-specific dynamics determine both onset risk and remedy effectiveness.

\paragraph{Independent configuration effects.}
The multi-rate configuration ($\dt{=}2$ subsampling, $H{=}8$) imposes performance costs independent of CIVO: frozen and removed embedding controls, which never trigger CIVO (0/13 seeds), achieve only $29$--$31$\% of baseline eval (Table~\ref{tab:intervention_hierarchy}). Practitioners considering temporal subsampling should anticipate performance costs even when CIVO is successfully prevented.

